From: swibrow <15628653+swibrow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 05:53:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Disable GPU persistence through a host-root
 nvidia-persistenced

disableGPUPersistenceMode only looks for the nvidia-persistenced socket under
the driver root. On hosts whose driver root is not / but which run the daemon
from the host (e.g. Talos: driver under /usr/local, socket under /run), the
daemon is reported as not running and keeps its handle on the GPU, so the
vfio-pci rebind cannot proceed. When the socket is absent under the driver
root but present under the host root, disable persistence mode with the host
driver's nvidia-smi run chrooted into the host root. This is best effort: on
failure it logs and proceeds as before.

Hosts whose persistenced socket is under the driver root take the unchanged
path.

Signed-off-by: swibrow <15628653+swibrow@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit ce050107f65597e9be1c7be1251c26ec06a30e1d)
